02:05:44,900 --> 02:06:02,620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: across income growths, or what's called income deciles, you see that households' incomes increased by almost, in nominal terms, over 20% in those periods.

1546
02:06:02,620 --> 02:06:09,800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It was a period, quite unusual, I would say, because it was a period of low inflation.

1547
02:06:10,840 --> 02:06:14,600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Income growth was quite widespread across.

1548
02:06:14,900 --> 02:06:16,520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Households.

1549
02:06:17,420 --> 02:06:20,880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So it was not an inequitable growth.

1550
02:06:22,220 --> 02:06:29,380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You can see the same percentage growth across the households' income classes.

1551
02:06:31,420 --> 02:06:37,940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And yes, and the labor market was also at its best.

1552
02:06:38,820 --> 02:06:43,920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It was a period when unemployment was declining, underemployment was declining.

1553
02:06:43,920 --> 02:07:05,020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The 2026 is a different story because the Middle East conflict, the oil price, sharp price, oil price increases, the deceleration of growth because of the scandal, partly because of scandal and the high inflation.

1554
02:07:05,420 --> 02:07:09,900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So some of those gains could have been eroded.

1555
02:07:10,160 --> 02:07:10,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Wipe out.

1556
02:07:10,600 --> 02:07:13,020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I don't think it is wipe out.

1557
02:07:13,020 --> 02:07:15,060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But I don't think, I really don't think that's wipe out.

1558
02:07:15,400 --> 02:07:20,680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But could have been eroded by those high inflation.

1559
02:07:21,140 --> 02:07:28,760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And now, unemployment is also beginning to, beginning, has also increased in recent quarters.

1560
02:07:30,100 --> 02:07:32,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Just one more question on the...

1561
02:07:32,940 --> 02:07:35,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, before it skips my mind, I follow up.

1562
02:07:36,860 --> 02:07:42,860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Where is the country headed in the next two years in terms of the, or using the following indicators?

1563
02:07:43,020 --> 02:07:51,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Inflation, national debt, atsaka yung peso versus the U.S. dollar and other currencies?

1564
02:07:53,820 --> 02:08:10,860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The last one is quite difficult to know, Your Honor, because the value of the peso does not depend just on our actions, but also actions of other countries.

1565
02:08:10,860 --> 02:08:12,860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Now that the Fed is strengthening.

1566
02:08:13,020 --> 02:08:26,280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's raising its policy rates, you would expect a lot of pressure on the peso because dollar-denominated assets will become now much more attractive.

1567
02:08:26,280 --> 02:08:42,540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, but there are other, of course, factors that how investors and our local population, both consumers and producers, see the future.

1568
02:08:43,020 --> 02:09:04,580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that if we can, as I keep saying, that if we can address the common variables that have led to this pessimism, to this negative sentiments that happened in the last quarters, three quarters, we could be on a recovery.

1569
02:09:06,580 --> 02:09:12,580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, I think that there are some good news.

1570
02:09:13,020 --> 02:09:30,900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That happened lately, and I hope that that will temper now the sentiments, and I hope that there will are emerging solutions to the Middle East conflict, because that's the big uncertainty in the world economy right now.

1571
02:09:31,540 --> 02:09:41,700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We were expecting just a few months ago or a few weeks ago that oil prices would finally be at $80 per barrel.

1572
02:09:41,700 --> 02:09:42,700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But now it's back to...

1573
02:09:43,020 --> 02:09:48,620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To 100% because of, you know, certain actions that outside of our control.

1574
02:09:48,800 --> 02:09:51,880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, it's really a very uncertain world.

1575
02:09:53,040 --> 02:09:55,900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You know, that's the least that I could say.

1576
02:09:57,020 --> 02:10:02,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What's our projected national debt in June of 2028?

1577
02:10:02,460 --> 02:10:07,120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We are still working on a fiscal consolidation.

1578
02:10:07,120 --> 02:10:12,500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As you can see in the budget, the budget, the increase in the budget was very...

1579
02:10:13,020 --> 02:10:15,160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Small.

1580
02:10:15,340 --> 02:10:18,500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In fact, in real terms, it's likely flat.

1581
02:10:18,780 --> 02:10:20,060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's more like a flat, no?

1582
02:10:21,640 --> 02:10:30,820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Just to make sure that we are managing our fiscal issues, the fiscal space.

1583
02:10:30,820 --> 02:10:41,820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that we have agreed among the economic managers and discussed with the president that we need to...

1584
02:10:43,020 --> 02:10:45,400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To strong...

1585
02:10:45,400 --> 02:10:52,660
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To reorient our borrowing, to focus only on capital outlay and infrastructure, for example.

1586
02:10:54,660 --> 02:10:55,260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah.

1587
02:10:56,060 --> 02:11:04,840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Kasi parang [unclear] na tayo ng borrowing even for MOOE, ano?

1588
02:11:04,840 --> 02:11:07,340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I mean, some countries don't do that.

1589
02:11:07,420 --> 02:11:09,260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: They only borrow for capital outlay.

1590
02:11:09,260 --> 02:11:12,260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I think that that's a direction that we should take.

1591
02:11:12,520 --> 02:11:12,860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And...

1592
02:11:12,860 --> 02:11:13,000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And...

1593
02:11:13,020 --> 02:11:18,740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we are taking. And our fiscal consolidation program is geared for that.

1594
02:11:19,340 --> 02:11:23,020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Hopefully, there will be no extra pressure for us.

1595
02:11:23,360 --> 02:11:27,240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The problem is really our vulnerability energy.

1596
02:11:28,160 --> 02:11:37,620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Because we have little space that whenever, you know, world prices rise, we are hit quickly.

1597
02:11:37,620 --> 02:11:42,620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Because we don't have the kind of energy situation that our neighbors...

1598
02:11:43,020 --> 02:11:43,340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: have.

1599
02:11:44,760 --> 02:11:45,580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Sir [unclear].

1600
02:11:45,720 --> 02:11:46,420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you, Senator Kiko.

1601
02:11:46,420 --> 02:11:46,780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you.

1602
02:11:46,800 --> 02:11:47,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, sir, Senator Pangilinan

1603
02:11:47,200 --> 02:11:50,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Just a few more questions.

1604
02:11:51,160 --> 02:11:52,220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You know, we...

1605
02:11:52,220 --> 02:11:53,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The anti-agric...

1606
